  "worked_solution": "The notation $f:X\\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our functions.\n\n- The codomain of $p$ is $(-2,2],$ the interval from $-2$ to $2$ (including $2$ but not including $-2$).\n\n- The codomain of $q$ is $[-2,2),$ the interval from $-2$ to $2$ (including $-2$ but not including $2$).\n\n- The codomain of $r$ is $(-2,2],$ the interval from $-2$ to $2$ (including $2$ but not including $-2$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
